# Draft of the rules for the shapes, to add to ids/climate-change-kg/.htaccess
# of perma-id/w3id.org, before the rule that sends everything else to the website.
#
#   https://w3id.org/climate-change-kg/shapes        the set of shapes
#   https://w3id.org/climate-change-kg/shapes/       (the same, with the slash)
#   https://w3id.org/climate-change-kg/shapes/<name> a shape (e.g. Resource) or a file (e.g. generic.ttl)
#
# Turtle (or RDF in general) is requested: shapes.ttl, the combined file. Anything else (a browser): the landing
# page. The files of the shapes, <name>.ttl, are served as they are.
#
# SITE is the GitHub Pages site of the repository (to check: it follows the name of the repository).

Options +FollowSymLinks
RewriteEngine On

# The shapes by content negotiation (the shapes themselves, as the files, have no document of their own)
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/turtle [OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/rdf\+xml [OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/ld\+json
RewriteRule ^shapes(/[^.]*)?$ https://hacid-project.github.io/climate-services-kg/shapes/shapes.ttl [R=303,L]

# The files
RewriteRule ^shapes/([A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.ttl)$ https://hacid-project.github.io/climate-services-kg/shapes/$1 [R=302,L]

# The landing page (also for the IRIs of the single shapes)
RewriteRule ^shapes(/.*)?$ https://hacid-project.github.io/climate-services-kg/shapes/ [R=303,L]
